* bl-a2-cs-cg-split: CS + CG split-pair balun (single-in / diff-out).
* Lineage: textbook single-ended-to-differential CS/CG split (the class
* baseline / contrast family to the noise-cancelling balun). Bench-v1 anchor.
* Structure-only, ZERO component values.
* Harness convention (diff3 3-port): port1 = single-ended RF in = VIN1;
* port2 = INVERTING output leg = VOUT1; port3 = NON-INVERTING output leg =
* VOUT2 (harness/diff3 net-name convention). Structure: input DC-blocked (C1)
* to split node n1. CS branch -- NM1 GATE at n1, drain is the INVERTING leg
* (anti-phase): tuned load L1 to VDD, DC-blocked (C2) to VOUT1. CG branch --
* NM2 SOURCE at n1 (1/gm), drain is the NON-INVERTING leg (in-phase): tuned
* load L2 to VDD, DC-blocked (C3) to VOUT2; NM2 gate AC-grounded (Cg) and
* mirror-biased; NM2 source DC-returned to VSS through R4. Published
* in-topology BIAS NETWORK: current-mirror reference (R1 -> diode NM3) biases
* the CS gate (feed R2) and the CG gate (feed R3).
* Approved 2026-09-14 (bench round 1, "approve all").
C C1 VIN1 n1
NMOS NM1 n2 n1 VSS VSS
L L1 VDD n2
C C2 n2 VOUT1
NMOS NM2 n3 n4 n1 VSS
R R4 n1 VSS
L L2 VDD n3
C C3 n3 VOUT2
R R1 VDD n5
NMOS NM3 n5 n5 VSS VSS
R R2 n5 n1
R R3 n5 n4
C Cg n4 VSS
